     1,
     "Hi,\r<br>\r<br>When I read data directly from myDiff results, e.g. \r<br>\r<br>source(&quot;<a href=\"http://edmr.googlecode.com/files/eDMR.v.0.4.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://edmr.googlecode.com/files/eDMR.v.0.4.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234936569000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0sNh3O1DRU_rjuBXmci3G7\">http://edmr.googlecode.com/files/eDMR.v.0.4.R</a>&quot;)\r<br>myDiff=fast.read(&quot;control_test.bed&quot;)\r<br>Now myDiff is data.frame class, how to convert methylDiff object?\r<br>\r<br>Best,\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>Xiuying\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "pooqjcu2kTkJ",
   "from": "Altuna Akalin",
   "author": "ab8277113f65c05e",
   "date": "2013-08-23T09:31:30Z",
   "subject": "Re: how to convert data.frame to methylDiff object",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div>You can create methylDiff object with the new() function, but I do not recommend doing this. The safest way to create it is via calculateDiffMeth() function.</div><div><br></div><div>If you make sure the data frame part of the methylDiff object has exactly the same structure (column names, column order, column classes), then you can do the following. <b>But I again discourage using this method because if you construct the object in a wrong way, the downstream analysis may not work</b>. </div><div><br></div><div>Below, <b>x</b> is the data frame that has the same structure as a regular methylDiff object. To see an example of a methylDiff object, do <div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">methylKit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">methylKit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\">methylDiff</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">obj</span></div></code></div><br></div><div>The rest of the attributes are self explanatory, you can check the vignette/ function help to understand what they mean if you are not sure.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Monaco,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding-left:4px;vertical-align:top\"><span style=\"color:#000\">obj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#008\">new</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;methylDiff&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ids</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;test1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;control1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                       assembly</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;hg18&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">context</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;CpG&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-left:4px;vertical-align:top\"><span style=\"color:#000\">                              treatment</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\">destranded</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">resolution</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;region&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-left:4px;vertical-align:top\"><span style=\"color:#000\">                           </span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></code></div><br><br></div><div> Best,<br></div><div>Altuna</div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">When I read data directly from myDiff results, e.g. \r\n<br>\r\n<br>source(&quot;<a href=\"http://edmr.googlecode.com/files/eDMR.v.0.4.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://edmr.googlecode.com/files/eDMR.v.0.4.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234936573000&amp;usg=AOvVaw26KcAfFrWJIH4s7wP2f2ze\">http://edmr.googlecode.com/files/eDMR.v.0.4.R</a>&quot;)\r\n<br>myDiff=fast.read(&quot;control_test.bed&quot;)\r\n<br>Now myDiff is data.frame class, how to convert methylDiff object?\r\n<br>\r\n<br>Best,\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>Xiuying\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
